  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.8.0 production hardening freezes the existing public contract while strengthening lifetime, concurrency, cancellation, lifecycle, failure-recovery, ownership, and scale behavior. Logical screens, windows, pads, and viewports remain single-writer; one Terminal-owned event consumer may wait concurrently with serialized refresh/output activity; disposal unblocks pending DCurses input/lifecycle waits without discarding Terminal decoder state; output uncertainty invalidates retained physical knowledge for safe retry; repeated rich-input/full-screen ownership cycles restore deterministically; and bounded large-pad, large-screen, sparse-refresh, and no-op workloads are exercised. The 0.8 release adds no public API. PR validation covers Windows x64/ARM64, Linux x64/ARM64, macOS x64/ARM64, net8.0/net9.0/net10.0, and package/fresh-consumer validation. Dependencies remain Icod.Terminal 1.4.0 and Icod.TermInfo 1.10.0.",
